Plain-language summary (the license texts above are what count; this summary is
not part of them):

  - Anyone may use VDWT under the AGPL-3.0, including commercially, if they
    comply with it: in short, if you distribute VDWT or software built with it,
    or let users interact with it over a network, you must make the complete
    corresponding source code of that software available under the AGPL-3.0.

  - A company with fewer than 100 people (employees and contractors, counting
    its whole corporate group) and less than 1,000,000 USD (2019, adjusted for
    inflation) revenue in the prior tax year may use VDWT under the PolyForm
    Small Business License, including in closed-source products, without
    releasing its own source code.

  - Everyone else who wants to use VDWT without the AGPL-3.0's source-code
    obligations needs a commercial license. Internal evaluation for up to 90
    days is free for any company; see COMMERCIAL.md.

